---

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:860px">
    <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
    <h1>Questions a principal actually asks</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:14px">
      The ones that come up in the first meeting, answered including where the
      answer is no.
    </p>

    <div style="margin-top:30px">
<details class="q">
        <summary>What happens to our data if we stop paying?<span class="q__m" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <p>
          It stays yours. Export everything at any time, including after you have
          cancelled, in a plain readable format. We do not hold records to ransom
          and there is no charge for taking your own data out.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="q">
        <summary>Does it work when the internet goes down?<span class="q__m" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <p>
          Attendance does. Teachers can keep marking the register and it syncs when
          the connection returns. Fee collection needs the connection, because two
          clerks taking cash offline would issue two receipts with the same number,
          and a fee book with duplicate numbers is worse than a fee book you have to
          wait five minutes for.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="q">
        <summary>Can a clerk change a receipt after it is printed?<span class="q__m" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <p>
          No. Nothing is deleted or edited. A mistake is corrected by a reversal
          entry, so both lines stay in the ledger with a reason and the name of the
          person who made the correction. Receipt numbers are issued in an unbroken
          sequence, so a missing number is itself visible.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="q">
        <summary>Can parents see other children's information?<span class="q__m" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <p>
          A parent login reaches only that family's own children: their fee balance,
          their receipts, their attendance and their results once you publish them.
          It cannot reach any other family, and it cannot reach anything you have
          not published.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="q">
        <summary>We already have years of records in Excel. Can we move them?<span class="q__m" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <p>
          Yes. Students, staff and opening balances import from a spreadsheet. Bring
          us the file you already keep and we will map it with you rather than asking
          you to retype a school.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="q">
        <summary>What about results that are not final yet?<span class="q__m" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <p>
          Marks stay unpublished until you publish them, and a result card can be
          withheld for a single student, for example while a fee matter is settled.
          Parents see nothing until you decide they should.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="q">
        <summary>Is there a manual, or do you train us?<span class="q__m" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <p>
          Both. The <a href="/guide.html">handbook</a> is sixteen chapters with real
          screenshots taken from the software itself, and it is free to read now,
          before you buy anything. It covers the office screens, the parent portal
          and what to do when something is entered wrong. We also walk your clerk
          through the first month's fee run on a call.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="q">
        <summary>Is it in Urdu?<span class="q__m" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <p>
          The screens are in English. Anything you type is accepted and printed in
          Urdu, including names, addresses and remarks, so a certificate or a fee
          receipt can carry Urdu text. A full Urdu interface is not built yet, and we
          would rather say so than imply otherwise.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

